WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:11.962
A complex sound is a sum of partials. The lowest is the fundamental; if the others are whole multiples of it, they are called harmonics.

2
00:00:14.711 --> 00:00:22.980
If the partials are not whole multiples, they are inharmonic. The wave stops repeating and the sound recalls a bell or a metal plate.

3
00:00:26.031 --> 00:00:34.317
The difference shows in the waveform: the harmonic sum repeats the same cycle every 5 milliseconds; the inharmonic one keeps changing.

4
00:00:35.018 --> 00:00:43.129
Timbre depends on which partials are present and how strong they are. Moving a single partial changes the color of the sound, even though the pitch stays at the fundamental.
